{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nThe security hotfix is complete. Here's the summary:\n\n**Fix Applied: `repo/export_api/storage.py`**\n\nThe vulnerability was in `_normalize_requested_path` which only performed a single `unquote()` pass, allowing double-encoded paths like `%252e%252e%252f` to bypass the `..` check.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **Iterative decoding**: Repeatedly decode the path until stable, handling double/triple encoding\n2. **Absolute path rejection**: Added check for Unix absolute paths (`/`) and Windows drive-qualified paths (`C:`)\n3. **Path containment**: Uses resolved absolute path prefix check with trailing `/` to prevent directory name collisions\n\n**All request samples validated:**\n- ✓ `REQ-legit-nested`: Nested exports work correctly\n- ✓ `REQ-encoded-dotdot`: Percent-encoded traversal blocked\n- ✓ `REQ-double-encoded`: Double-encoded traversal blocked\n- ✓ `REQ-mixed-slash`: Mixed slash traversal blocked\n- ✓ `REQ-absolute`: Absolute path escapes blocked\n- ✓ `REQ-drive-qualified`: Drive-qualified paths blocked\n\n**Artifacts created:**\n- `audit/triage_note.json` - Triage documentation\n- `repo/ops/deploy_hotfix.json` - Deployment instructions\n\n**Validation:**\n- `cnb55-hotfix-artifacts validate` - Passed\n- `make test` - All 4 tests pass"}}
